  // buffers must hold a count of each element for the last owner's element
  // walk to free them once. Null / low-address / immortal buffers are skipped
  // like the deep-free walks skip them, and each element takes rc_inc's guards
  // inline: a tagged or low pointer and a static box's negative count are
  // left alone. It makes no call, so it needs no saved register: %rsi / %rdx
  // hold len / i and %rcx / %edi the element and its count.
