    // b: the self-append's path when a's block cannot take b. The block is
    // sized at twice a's length in words or the grown string's, whichever is
    // more, rounded to its class, so an accumulator re-copies its prefix once
    // per doubling; a's capacity is not the measure, since a shared a is
    // copied on every append. a is read, not released; the caller releases its unit.
    // __fern_str_grow_fresh_range(a@32, s@24, lo@16, hi@8) appends s's bytes
    // [lo, hi) the same way and traps on a range outside s, as the slice the
    // concatenation built would have. Both entries hand the body the source
    // bytes in %rdx and their count in %rsi.
    s = s.write("__fn___fern_str_grow_fresh:\n");
